# Nora release

Use this path when the user asks to publish the current version. Do not follow `docs/VPS.md` for it: that file describes the old 24nutrition host. This chat is https://aimods.site and https://www.aimods.site on server Nora. Do not publish this checkout over https://24ainews.site unless the user asks; that site is a different app.

Stay on branch `hybrid`. Do not create a branch. Remote: https://github.com/mediasevenlab/noraai.git. The previous remote remains `ai-news`.

## Git

- Inspect `git status`, `git diff`, and recent commit messages. Commit only this task's files.
- Never commit `.env`, `.scratch`, or release archives.
- `webapp/src/pages.tsx` often looks modified from line endings. If its diff is empty, do not add it.
- PowerShell commit: `git commit -m @'` … `'@`
- Push the same branch: `git push origin hybrid`.
- Production receives only what is already committed. Uncommitted edits are not in the archive.

## Production

SSH as `deploy-aimods` to `nora-aimods-wan` (port 2222). From the office, the same user on `nora-aimods`. Do not log in as `norton`, `nora`, or `root`.

You may only change files in `/srv/apps/aimods`. Do not touch other apps, nginx, certificates, or DNS. Host nginx already proxies the site to `127.0.0.1:18007`. Do not change that port. The web container listens on port 80 and is published as `127.0.0.1:18007:80`.

Do not run `docker` or `docker compose` directly. The only start command is `sudo nora-ctl aimods up` (`docker compose up -d` without `--build`; Compose builds a missing tag itself). Do not run `nora-ctl aimods pull`: images are local and are not pulled from a registry.

Server directory: `/srv/apps/aimods`. Sources live in `app/` — an unpacked archive, not a git repo. In `compose.yml` the tags are `nora-aimods-backend:<short sha>` and `nora-aimods-web:<short sha>`. The web image is `deploy/nora/web.Dockerfile`; it serves the landing and the app and proxies `/api` and `/health` to the backend. `RELEASE_SHA` is the full 40-character sha. Postgres data stays in `./data/postgres`. The backend joins the external Docker network `nora-llm_default` so speech is `http://stt:8080` and search is `http://search:8080`.

1. Take the short and full sha of current `HEAD`.
2. `git archive --format=tar -o .scratch/release-<short sha>.tar HEAD`
3. Copy the archive to the server and unpack it into `app/`.
4. Set both image tags to the new short sha and write the full sha to `RELEASE_SHA`.
5. `sudo nora-ctl aimods up`
6. `sudo nora-ctl aimods ps`: backend healthy, web on `127.0.0.1:18007`, both containers on the new tag.

In PowerShell, wrap remote `ssh` commands in single quotes so `$(...)` does not run locally. Do not print `.env` contents.

The web image build runs `tsc` and Vite. A type error fails the whole web image even if the backend image already built.

As of this instruction, GitHub and production publish from branch `hybrid` of https://github.com/mediasevenlab/noraai.git. Re-check `HEAD` before the next release.
